      "content": "so you're saying the income-based model is the better one. but what about people who argue that a lottery is the only way to be truly fair because it treats everyone exactly the same? a lot of people think picking based on income is just social engineering and it's actually unfair to families who are just barely above the cutoff. isn't that just as big of an equity issue?",
